Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:08:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] SystemUI: hold AOD at the dimmed brightness until it
 has animated in

After a screen timeout, clampToDimBrightnessForScreenOff() keeps the
first doze brightness at or below the dimmed screen, but only while the
doze machine is INITIALIZED. The AOD light sensor reports a few
milliseconds later, after DOZE_AOD has started, and its brightness is
applied straight away. In a lit room (about 10-20 lux on a Pixel 11 Pro
XL) that takes the panel from 0.5 nits to 10 nits while the
GONE -> AOD transition is still showing the app fading out, so the
screen flashes brighter for about a second.

After a timeout, hold the doze brightness at or below the dimmed level
until the keyguard transition has finished in AOD, then apply the latest
light sensor reading. A 2 s fallback releases the hold if AOD never
reports finishing. Power button sleeps are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
